Lynda Weinman was born in 1955 and graduated from The Evergreen State College in 1976. She taught herself to use computers by reading the manual for an Apple II. She worked in film as a special-effects animator, on movies such as *Star Trek V* and *RoboCop 2*.

## Designing web graphics

From 1989 to 1996 she taught digital media and motion graphics at ArtCenter College of Design in Pasadena. In the mid-1990s she noticed there were few good resources for designers moving to the web. Her book *Designing Web Graphics* is often credited as the first book about building websites from a visual designer's point of view.

## lynda.com

What started in 1995 as a simple website for her students and readers grew into one of the first big online learning companies.

- **1995:** Launched lynda.com as a free web resource for her students.
- **1997:** Incorporated lynda.com with her husband, Bruce Heavin.
- **2000s:** Turned lynda.com into an online library of video courses on design, software and business.
- **2015:** LinkedIn bought lynda.com for $1.5 billion. It later became LinkedIn Learning.

She has since returned to art. Since 2020 she has explored 3D clay printing, exhibiting sculptures and vessels made with 3D printers.

